# Copy this file to .env and add your key (never commit .env).
# ./scripts/setup.sh does this for you and validates the key before writing it.

# ── Your Novoads API key ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Format: novo_ followed by 64 hex characters.
# Create one at https://novoads.ai/dashboard/settings?tab=api
# Need an account? Start your $1 trial:
#   https://novoads.ai/?utm_source=claude-code&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=skill-pack
NOVOADS_API_KEY=novo_your_key_here

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override only if you were given a different host. The default is correct for
# every account. This is the HOST ONLY — callers append /v1/…, so no trailing
# slash and no /v1 here.
# NOVOADS_BASE_URL=https://api.novoads.ai

# ── Meta Ads (meta-ad-builder shared skill — OPTIONAL) ───────────────────────
# Powers shared/skills/meta-ad-builder/ — publishing creatives as Meta ads.
# Nothing here is needed to GENERATE anything. Leave it alone until you want to
# publish; you can also just ask to publish and follow what the skill prints —
# shared/skills/meta-ad-builder/scripts/check-meta-env.sh uncomments the two
# required lines for you, opens this file, and says where each value comes from.
# Every ad created by the skill is PAUSED — you launch manually in Ads Manager.
#
# CHECK FIRST: the Meta app issuing the token must be published (Live). A
# development-mode app passes every credential check and then fails at ad
# creation with code 100 / subcode 1885183. Allowlisting the ad account does not
# work around it (tested live 2026-08-03) — publish the app in App Dashboard.
#
# The two REQUIRED values, and where each comes from:
#
#  META_ACCESS_TOKEN  a long-lived token carrying the ads_management scope
#    specifically. ads_read alone passes /me and then dies at ad creation.
#    Graph API Explorer:  https://developers.facebook.com/tools/explorer
#      (pick your app, add ads_management, generate, then extend it to 60 days
#      at https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug/accesstoken)
#    Non-expiring alternative: Business Settings → Users → System Users.
#
#  META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID  the ad account the ads are created in. From the Ads
#    Manager account picker, or the act_… segment of any Ads Manager URL. The
#    act_ prefix is optional. The token's user needs a role on this account.
#
# The four OPTIONAL ones, all safe to leave commented:
#
#  META_PAGE_ID     the Facebook Page the ad runs as (Page → About → Page ID).
#                   Without it, deploy-ad.py needs --page-id on the command line.
#  META_IG_USER_ID  the linked Instagram account, for Instagram placements.
#  META_PIXEL_ID    from Events Manager → Data Sources, for conversion tracking.
#  META_API_VERSION Graph API version. Leave commented for the default, v23.0.
#
# META_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_long_lived_token_here
# META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=act_1234567890
# META_PAGE_ID=
# META_IG_USER_ID=
# META_PIXEL_ID=
# META_API_VERSION=v23.0
